     "result_text_tail": "M build in about 17 months. Pro reaches the 105% retention target on its own only if at least 26% of accounts move.\n- **Margin:** company margin stays at 75% or above only if Pro accounts average under about 5,300 AI requests a month. Accounts that paid in the beta used 6,800, so the allowance is essential.\n\n**Changes after an independent review** of the draft: it showed that waiting also gives up about $257K of Pro contribution per quarter, and that the 14% and 46% rates were measured at $149, so they don't set a floor or ceiling for Pro. Both are now on the slides, and the January check became gate 3 of the four launch gates.\n\n**Choices I made for you:**\n- Audience: the CEO and executive team, deciding whether to approve the launch.\n- Theme: navy.\n- I approved my own storyline.\n- Assumption to confirm with Engineering: the rewrite needs these 14 engineers only through Q2 2027. If it needs them longer, Copilot slips past Q4 2027.\n- I treated the $0.6M of platform cost as cost of revenue, which is the more cautious choice for the margin test.\n\nThe deck has 19 slides, 12 of them content. All 121 numbers trace to the briefing pack or a calculation shown in the workbook, and no placeholders remain. A possible next step is a version of the timing slide that shows how the answer moves with the share of churn the rewrite removes.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- brightwork-dispatch-copilot.pptx\n- brightwork-dispatch-copilot-sources.xlsx\n\nThe spec and build script are in `./work/`."
    }
